      "nodeId": "n3",
      "text": "AI could replace equivalent of 300 million jobs - report.",
      "contextBefore": "",
      "contextAfter": " Artificial intelligence (AI) could replace the equivalent of 300 million full-time jobs, a report by investment bank Goldman Sachs says. It could replace a quarter of work tasks in the US and Europe ",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 57,
      "extractSha256": "cc873de4283633cbb7596cb4aa814d9e1e48b7fe4de168ff4554b93d4356d2da",
      "windowSha256": "0dd6422446875668e35114981035da05d9462e5c229e4e5de8bf02a87e98b200",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-17T06:27:17.452Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20230328164108/https://www.bbc.com/news/technology-65102150",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "nodeId": "n4",
      "text": "Around the world, as many as 300 million jobs could be affected, the report says.",
      "contextBefore": "In the U.S., \"of those occupations which are exposed, most have a significant - but partial - share of their workload (25-50%) that can be replaced,\" Goldman Sachs analysts said in the resarch paper. ",
      "contextAfter": " Changes to labor markets are therefore likely - although historically, technological progress doesn't just make jobs redundant, it also creates new ones. The use of AI technology could also boost lab",
      "start": 664,
      "end": 745,
      "extractSha256": "cb06a5916abdde7c4c01b9377caf7997aac222ce97ab5b61d7ae21c3e3fb06e9",
